  "lines-and-slope.dg.psSigns": "The slope is right, but watch the signs in <b><i class=\"vr\">y</i> − <i class=\"vr\">y<sub>1</sub></i> = <i class=\"vr\">m</i>(<i class=\"vr\">x</i> − <i class=\"vr\">x<sub>1</sub></i>)</b>: the point’s coordinates are <i>subtracted</i>, so a negative coordinate turns into a +.",
  "lines-and-slope.dg.signB": "The slope is right, but check the sign of b, the plain number.",
